# IDENT: Transfer IDENT code of interrupting device - 10-bit mask instruction
# YAML: mask "1111_1111_1100_0000", opcode "0143600" (octal)
# Transfer highest priority device IDENT code to A register
#
# Transfers IDENT code of interrupting device with highest priority
# on specified level to A register. Used in interrupt handlers.
#
# Supported interrupt levels:
# - PL10: Level 10 (value 000004)
# - PL11: Level 11 (value 000011)
# - PL12: Level 12 (value 000022)
# - PL13: Level 13 (value 000043)
#
# P-code implementation:
# A = get_highest_priority_ident(level_code);
# # Returns device identification code for interrupt handling
#
# SLEIGH Limitation: Cannot implement due to 10-bit mask
# Manual implementation would require sub-tables for level selection
# :IDENT level_code {
#     A = interrupt_system_ident[level_code];
#     # Read device IDENT from interrupt controller
# }